# Compiled CLI binary at repo root only — anchored so it does not match
# directories named "irgo" (e.g. the android com/irgo package or cmd/irgo).
/irgo

# Compiled example binaries at repo root
/todo
/gohtmx

# Dev server reload marker
.reload-signal

# Build outputs. These were carve-outs because build/macos/ held tracked shell
# scripts; those are gone (irgo package macos does the work), so the whole
# directory is generated now.
/build/
/dist/

# Node dependencies
node_modules/

# The templ docs site is a nested module; its generated output follows the same
# rules as any irgo project.
docs-templ/build/
docs-templ/tmp/
docs-templ/dist/
docs-templ/static/css/output.css
docs-templ/templates/*_templ.go

# Generated by `irgo app build ios|android` for gomobile, and full of absolute
# paths from whichever machine ran it — never committed.
go.work
go.work.sum
# Built by `irgo app build android`. The project template has always ignored
# this; this repository was committing 14 MB of it per rebuild.
android/Example/app/libs/*.aar
build/ios/Irgo.xcframework/

# The rules this repository's own template gives every project, minus the ones
# that only make sense there: a generated project's ios/Example and
# android/Example are scaffolded output, while this repository maintains them
# as source.
#
# It had none of these, so two generated _templ.go files and a built
# output.css were committed here — in the repository that tells projects not
# to commit exactly those.
bin/
build/
tmp/
vendor/
package-lock.json
bun.lock
*_templ.go
static/css/output.css
android/Example/app/libs/irgo.aar
dist/
irgo.package.local.toml
*.irgo-bak
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
build-errors.log
.env
.env.local
# .claude holds per-machine assistant settings, which are personal.
#
# .claude/skills is the exception and is committed. It is the copy every irgo
# project is served from, so a skill that is not in the repository is a skill
# nobody gets — including the assistants working on irgo itself.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# The examples are separate modules, so every build syncs its own copy of the
# skills into each of them. Committing those would put the same 74 KB Datastar
# reference in this repository three times, and the copy that matters here is
# the one above — this repository's own, which is also what every project is
# served from.
#
# A real project does commit its copy; the scaffolded .gitignore says so and
# why. The difference is that a project has no canonical copy of its own.
examples/*/.claude/
docs-templ/.claude/
.claude/

# Written by `mise run setup` so the tasks survive a switch to a branch cut
# from main, which does not carry mise.toml. Local, never committed.
mise.local.toml
